%SIXMD 1
# @?MKSWAP - SAFELY PROVISION OFFLINE AUXST1 SWAP IMAGES

## DESCRIPTION

MKSWAP IS A HOST-SIDE OFFLINE IMAGE TOOL, NOT A NATIVE DAIMOS COMMAND.
IT SHARES THE AUXST1 MEDIA FORMATTER WITH THE HOST MKAUXSTORE UTILITY.
IT DOES NOT ACCESS A LIVE DEVICE OR FORMAT MEDIA DURING GUEST BOOT.
SIXMD UPPERCASES MANUAL TEXT; ACTUAL HOST COMMAND OPTIONS AND
CONTROLLER VALUES MUST BE ENTERED IN LOWERCASE.

THE OPERATOR MUST SELECT THE EXACT CONTROLLER, UNIT, AND IMAGE.
CURRENT DAIMOS KINIT DISCOVERS ONLY UNIT ZERO OF DSK AND DRM; MKSWAP
THEREFORE REJECTS OTHER UNITS. A DRM IMAGE MUST CONTAIN 020000 BLOCKS;
A DSK IMAGE MUST CONTAIN 0130000 BLOCKS. EACH BLOCK IS 128 PDP-10
WORDS, STORED AS EIGHT LITTLE-ENDIAN BYTES PER WORD.

WITHOUT A FORMAT MODE, MKSWAP INSPECTS AN EXISTING AUXST1 DESCRIPTOR
AND REJECTS INVALID REGIONS OR OVERLAP. INSPECTION DOES NOT MODIFY
THE IMAGE. IT DOES NOT PROVE THE CONTENTS OF A BACKING REGION ARE
VALID SWAPPED PROCESS DATA.

FORMATTING CREATES A SWAP-ONLY AUXST1 LAYOUT WITHOUT A D6FS REGION.
THE BACKSTORE, OPTIONAL LOGSTORE, AND OPTIONAL CACHESTORE SIZES MUST
EXACTLY FILL THE SPACE AFTER DESCRIPTOR BLOCK ZERO. EACH REGION IS
CHECKED FOR PREEXISTING CONTENT BEFORE ANY WRITE. AN EXISTING
DESCRIPTOR, DBOOT HEADER, OR UNKNOWN NONEMPTY DATA IS NEVER ERASED.

AN OFFLINE DRM0 IMAGE OF 020000 BLOCKS CAN BE INSPECTED WITH:

    MKSWAP --CONTROLLER DRM --UNIT 0 --IMAGE DRM0.DSK

TO CHECK A NEW SWAP-ONLY LAYOUT, USE --FORMAT AND --DRY-RUN FIRST.
REPLACE --DRY-RUN WITH --CONFIRM-DESTRUCTIVE TO FORMAT AN EMPTY IMAGE.

## @?OPTIONS

### @?--CONTROLLER DRM OR DSK
SELECT THE PHYSICAL CONTROLLER CLASS THAT WILL OWN THE IMAGE.

### @?--UNIT 0
SELECT THE ONLY CURRENTLY SUPPORTED DISCOVERABLE UNIT.

### @?--IMAGE IMAGE
EXACT PATH TO A REGULAR HOST IMAGE FILE. SYMLINKS ARE REFUSED.

### @?--INSPECT
INSPECT AND VALIDATE AN EXISTING DESCRIPTOR. THIS IS THE DEFAULT.

### @?--FORMAT
REQUEST A NEW SWAP-ONLY AUXST1 DESCRIPTOR AND REGION LAYOUT.

### @?--BACKSTORE-BLOCKS N
REQUIRED POSITIVE SWAP REGION SIZE WHEN FORMATTING.

### @?--LOGSTORE-BLOCKS N
OPTIONAL LOG REGION SIZE; DEFAULT ZERO.

### @?--CACHE-BLOCKS N
OPTIONAL CACHE REGION SIZE; DEFAULT ZERO.

### @?--DRY-RUN
VALIDATE A PROPOSED FORMAT AND CONFIRM THE TARGET REGIONS ARE EMPTY.
NO IMAGE BYTES ARE CHANGED. USE WITH --FORMAT.

### @?--CONFIRM-DESTRUCTIVE
REQUIRED FOR A REAL FORMAT; CANNOT BE USED WITH --DRY-RUN.

## @?OPERANDS

### @?N
BLOCK COUNTS ACCEPT C NUMERIC NOTATION: LEADING ZERO IS OCTAL.

## @?EXIT STATUS

### @?0 - SUCCESS
### @?1 - I/O, VALIDATION, OR SAFETY CHECK FAILED
### @?2 - INVALID USAGE
